class Solution {
    public boolean search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int left = 0; 
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        // Binary search loop
        while (left <= right) {

            // Find middle index
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            // ✅ If target found
            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return true;
            }

            // ⚠️ Case 1: Duplicates (cannot decide sorted side)
            // Example: [2,2,2,3,2]
            if (nums[left] == nums[mid] && nums[mid] == nums[right]) {
                left++;   // shrink from left
                right--;  // shrink from right
            }

            // ✅ Case 2: Left half is sorted
            else if (nums[left] <= nums[mid]) {

                // Check if target lies in left sorted half
                if (nums[left] <= target && target < nums[mid]) {
                    right = mid - 1;   // search left side
                } else {
                    left = mid + 1;    // search right side
                }
            }

            // ✅ Case 3: Right half is sorted
            else {

                // Check if target lies in right sorted half
                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[right]) {
                    left = mid + 1;    // search right side
                } else {
                    right = mid - 1;   // search left side
                }
            }
        }

        // ❌ Target not found
        return false;
    }
}
🧠 Intuition (Simple)

At every step:

Try to find which half is sorted
Check if target lies in that half
Move accordingly
If duplicates block decision → shrink boundaries
⏱️ Time Complexity
Best case: O(1) → target found immediately
Average case: O(log n) → normal binary search
Worst case: O(n)
Happens when many duplicates
Example: [1,1,1,1,1,1,1]
💾 Space Complexity
O(1) (constant space)
No extra memory used, only variables
🔥 Final Takeaway

👉 This problem = Binary Search + Edge Case (Duplicates)
👉 The only tricky part is:

nums[left] == nums[mid] == nums[right]
